{
  "post_stream": {
    "posts": [
      {
        "id": 13934,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-12-02T21:28:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I've had a chance to play my first full game of Bottom of the 9th and think it is great. It helps that I like baseball, but what I enjoy the most is the Stare Down and the real time dice rolling.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I think a better solution could be found for some of the terms. Right now, the pitcher's die has three results: B for Ball, S for Strike, and C for Corner. After the batter has swung, the final result of a pitch can be Ball, Strike, and Contact.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>These terms have multiple problems:</p><ul>\n<li>Overloading: Both Ball and Strike are used in two different contexts.</li>\n<li>Confusion: C is used for Painting the Corner, but in part because of the first problem, players consistently think it means Contact.</li>\n</ul><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Suggestions:</p><ul>\n<li>Change the pitchers die terms from Ball/Strike to something like In-the-Zone/Out-of-the-Zone (IZ/OZ)</li>\n<li>Change the letter used for Painting the Corner to 'P'</li>\n</ul>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:45:52.971Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 1,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.2,
